In [[Caphiria]], '''Vestiary Laws''' ([[Caphiric Latin]]: '''''Leges Vestiariae''''') are a body of sumptuary legislation regulating dress, adornment, and personal appearance according to [[Stratification in Caphiria|social class]]. For much of Caphirian history, these laws served as the primary mechanism for making ''[[Stratification in Caphiria#Class (Ordo)|Ordo]]'' (legal class) visible in public life, prescribing what materials, colors, and garment constructions were permitted or forbidden to each stratum of society. While active enforcement largely ceased during the 19th century and formal prosecutions are now exceptionally rare, the Vestiary Laws remain technically valid imperial statute and continue to inform ceremonial dress requirements in official contexts.

