'''Corporate law in Caphiria''' encompasses the body of law governing the formation, operation, regulation, taxation, and dissolution of business entities within the [[Caphiria|Imperium of Caphiria]]. It is one of the most extensive and internally distinctive legal domains in [[Judiciary of Caphiria|Caphirian jurisprudence]], reflecting an economic philosophy known as ''[[Oeconomicum]]'' that rejects both pure state ownership and unfettered market capitalism in favor of a calibrated system in which strategic sectors are channeled through privileged corporate entities aligned with imperial objectives, while the broader commercial economy operates under a layered framework of statutory, regulatory, and professional controls. 

