{{Politics of Cartadania}}
'''Citizenship in Cartadania''' is a legal status conferred by the [[Constitution of Cartadania|Constitution]] and [[Law of Cartadania|laws]] of the [[Cartadania|republic]], entitling individuals to a set of defined rights, protections, responsibilities, and privileges. It functions as a foundational framework for the enjoyment of civil and political rights, including the rights to vote, to freedom of expression, to reside and work within the country, to access public services, and to participate in public life.

Cartadania operates under both {{wp|jus soli}} and {{wp|jus sanguinis}} principles. It is the only country in northern Sarpedon to excercise jus soli and citizenship is considered permanent and irrevocable except in cases of severe legal transgressions such as treason, perjury, or desertion. Citizenship is granted automatically to individuals born within the territory of Cartadania, including its airspace

{{Culture of Cartadania}}
'''Immigration to Cartadania''', both in the country's modern borders and the many political entities that preceded it, has occurred throughout the country's history. It has spiked during numerous phenomena and conflicts around the country and has allowed the nation to amass the ninth-largest population and fourth-largest economy on the planet. Today, Cartadania is one of the most popular destinations for immigrants in the world, and a majority go on to become [[Cartadanians|Cartadanian]] [[citizenship in Cartadania|citizens]].

