The '''Tribal Assembly''' was the primary lawmaking body within [[Great Levantia]], especially during the republican period.  In the tribal assembly, citizens were organized on the basis of the [[Vigintiquinque|twenty-five tribes]], kinship groups spread throughout the [[Adonerii]] colonies which established Great Levantia but were represented among the people of Urcepól. Each tribe voted separately and one after the other. In each tribe, decisions were made by majority vote and its decision counted as one vote regardless of how many electors each tribe held. Once a majority of tribes voted in the same way on a given measure, the voting ended and the matter was decided. In practice, the Assembly ratified acts of the Senate by giving its assent. Rarely did the Assembly act independently of the Senate as a lawmaking body. The Assembly was also responsible for the election of the various offices of state.

